SemCurSeg

This repository includes code from the following projects, each released under the Apache
License 2.0.

SimTxtSeg (Y. Xie, T. Zhou, Y. Zhou, G. Chen; MICCAI 2024)
https://github.com/xyx1024/SimTxtSeg
  Derived from SimTxtSeg: semcurseg/segmentor/ (network, dataset), tools/build_coco_boxes.py,
  tools/train_segmentor.py, tools/test_segmentor.py, configs/_base_/ and the MMDetection tool
  scripts. Changes:
  - segmentor/model.py, apfo.py: Adaptive Prompt Feature Optimizer (APFO) added.
  - segmentor/tvha.py: attention pooling of the caption tokens; positional encodings sized to the
    tokens used and not stored in checkpoints (values unchanged); adaptive global pooling in the
    channel attention; dropout registered as a module so that it is disabled in evaluation mode
    (SimTxtSeg created it inside forward(), where it stayed active at test time); unused layers removed.
  - segmentor/dataset.py: per-image captions and Stage 1 pseudo masks; files matched by name.
  - segmentor/loss.py: Dice + BCE on the predicted probabilities (SimTxtSeg applied MONAI's
    DiceCELoss, whose BCE term expects logits, to probabilities).
  - metrics.py: IoU is the Jaccard index (SimTxtSeg's iou_score returned half the Dice score).
  - tools/build_coco_boxes.py: rewritten, one box per connected component.

MMDetection (OpenMMLab)
https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection
  tools/train_cgtvcc.py, tools/test_cgtvcc.py, tools/dist_*_cgtvcc.sh and configs/_base_/ come from
  MMDetection 3.3.0 (an import path was added). semcurseg/scgm/curriculum.py and
  semcurseg/scgm/phrase_weighting.py subclass MMDetection's BaseDetDataset, GroundingDINO,
  GroundingDINOHead and FocalLoss.

Segment Anything (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
https://github.com/facebookresearch/segment-anything
  segment_anything/ is an unmodified copy.

Written for SemCurSeg: semcurseg/scgm/, semcurseg/sam_adapt/, semcurseg/segmentor/apfo.py,
semcurseg/metrics.py (HD95), tools/build_scgm_captions.py, tools/train_sam_adapt.py,
tools/stage1_inference.py, tools/eval_hd95.py and configs/cgtvcc_*.py.
